file tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_run.sh -- a fourth `capability_state()` arm, `day_shelf`, reading ROTA_DAY and git ls-files exactly as the guard's own scan does, with a missing git answering unknown so it runs
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri -- `capability day_shelf` on the rota_declared row, and sow_allow_reach's own capability comment moved back to the row it annotates
file tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_control.sh -- a git pen planting no shelf, an untracked log, and a committed one, the pen proven innocent, and the scan reading the new word off the runner's own arms
file tools/s/standing_equipment_witness.rish -- ten behaviors asserted BY NAME, since a named case reds when deleted where a total only shrinks
file construction/REDS.md -- booked and CLOSED as `%533` and folded to its own shelf on the same lap, since a peer's large row landed beside it and left the pin 2,692 over; booked `%529` from a spine reading shared_max=528, and the rebase found a peer had bound that number to an earlier stamp, so the row renumbered and the STAMP is what every citation of it already spelled
file construction/archive/REDS-fold-recital.md -- this lap's own fold line WITHDRAWN whole: written for %518 and %523, rewritten for %523 alone when a peer's earlier fold of %518 arrived, and dropped entirely when a second rebase brought a peer's fold of %523 with %527 and %528 beside it, stamped an hour before mine. The pin needed no fold from me in the end, because theirs had already bought the room
file construction/ITINERARY.md -- the account, the folded pointer, and %524's citation released from stamp to number now that the spine has bound it
file construction/archive/20260907-004225_itinerary-landed-accounts.md -- three landed BAKERY accounts folded whole, residues carried rather than lost
file construction/CHECKPOINTS.md -- the cairn for that fold, naming what it removed and where every word still reads
file construction/ITINERARY.md -- and one clause of a peer's account: a locally-tagged hash that resolves in no other clone, withheld so the claim stops promising a door nobody can open
file construction/archive/REDS-a-guard-shaped-by-the-clock-rows-533.md -- the shelf this row folded to, the only unambiguously CLOSED row standing and this seat's own, which is what let it fold with no peer to race
recommend keep-going -- the link wall is the next lap and its shape is decided: rule five on the debt trigger alone, since readme_reach_scan crawls the WORKTREE and a staged trigger would refuse a commit for an unstaged edit it does not carry. That is the one design choice, and it is why the rule wants its own lap on a file eight ships run.
